# Primer Dark for GNU dircolors (LS_COLORS)
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# LS_COLORS is read by ls, tree, fd, fish and bash completion, and eza when no
# eza theme overrides a kind. Load it from a shell startup file:
#     sh/bash:  eval "$(dircolors -b /path/to/primer-dark.dircolors)"
#     fish:     set -gx LS_COLORS (dircolors -c /path/to/primer-dark.dircolors | string split "'")[2]
# or copy it to ~/.dir_colors where a distribution profile script loads it.
#
# Kinds match cli/eza/theme.yml. Colors use 24-bit SGR sequences, so every
# terminal theme in this suite renders the exact Primer values. They are only
# emitted when the terminal advertises 24-bit color through COLORTERM or a
# direct-color TERM; elsewhere, such as the Linux console, LS_COLORS is empty
# and ls keeps its built-in colors.

COLORTERM ?*
TERM *-direct
TERM xterm-ghostty

# File kinds
RESET 0
DIR 01;38;2;68;147;248
LINK 38;2;57;197;207
